      "targetText": "3. Commute with the same positive square rootThe unique positive root of Gc² is Gc. Commutation with the argument passes to its continuous functional calculus.GC2=GC,[GC2,DC]=0⇒[GC,DC]=0.Corresponding Lean step  have hGcNonneg : 0 ≤ Gc := (ContinuousLinearMap.nonneg_iff_isPositive Gc).mpr hGc\n  have hRoot : CFC.sqrt (Gc*Gc)=Gc := CFC.sqrt_unique rfl hGcNonneg\n  have hLift : Commute Gc Dc := by\n    have h := hComplex.cfcₙ_nnreal NNReal.sqrt\n    change Commute (CFC.sqrt (Gc*Gc)) Dc at h\n    rwa [hRoot] at h\nLiteral compiled BODY span;exact preceding locals remain in scope.",
      "bodyVisibility": "visible",
      "bodyDisplay": "block",
      "closedLeanDetails": 1,
