      "targetText": "6. Consume the B23 coefficient identity at original inputsThe Test starts from the original potential and step inputs. The product of commuting selfadjoint operators is selfadjoint;multiplying the exact square identity by Inv² gives the coefficient identity.K=A0Inv=K∗,I+K2=(Γ02+A02)Inv2=Inv2.Corresponding Lean step  have hKself : IsSelfAdjoint (A0*Inv) := (hA0self.commute_iff hInvSelf).mp hCommInv\n  have hCoefficient : (1 : HP0 →L[ℝ] HP0)+(A0*Inv)*(A0*Inv)=Inv*Inv := by\n    have hFirst : (ΓP0*ΓP0)*(Inv*Inv)=(1 : HP0 →L[ℝ] HP0) := by\n      calc\n        (ΓP0*ΓP0)*(Inv*Inv)=ΓP0*((ΓP0*Inv)*Inv) := by noncomm_ring\n        _ = (1 : HP0 →L[ℝ] HP0) := by rw [hRight,one_mul,hRight]\n    have hSecond : (A0*Inv)*(A0*Inv)=(A0*A0)*(Inv*Inv) := by\n      calc\n        (A0*Inv)*(A0*Inv)=A0*((Inv*A0)*Inv) :=",
